From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:45:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 149/342] meson_header: the ODROID-C2 header's pins, who has
 them, their mux

A kernel module for the drivers that use pins of the 40-pin header
(meson_gpio, meson_i2c, the serial port's): the table of the header's
pins with a SoC pad, their alternate functions and the pin controller's
mux bits for them; claims, so that a pin has one user at a time (a
driver, or a program through meson_gpio), with a name and a team to show
who has it; and function selection under one lock, as the mux words are
shared. Pins 3 and 5 (I2C A, the RTC shield) aren't offered to
programs, nor pin 33's PWM (its controller's other channel sets a core
voltage). A boot module: meson_i2c needs it for the clock at boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
